INT. SYNERGY CLOSET - OFFICE SUPPLY ROOM - DAY

A converted broom closet with a laminated sign reading SYNERGY CLOSET: THINK BIG. Shelves of sticky notes and toner. Three colleagues stand shoulder to shoulder with nowhere to put their elbows: MORTIMER GRAY, fifties, regional director; LAKSHMI IYER, thirties, project lead; DUNCAN OKORO, twenties, intern.

MORTIMER
Right. Let's circle back on the circle-back.

LAKSHMI
We circled back last week.

MORTIMER
And what did we learn?

LAKSHMI
That we should circle back.

DUNCAN
Sorry, can I ask what the project is?

MORTIMER
The project is alignment.

DUNCAN
Aligned with what?

MORTIMER
With the vision.

LAKSHMI
Which is?

MORTIMER
It's in the deck.

LAKSHMI
The deck is forty slides and slide nine is a picture of a canoe.

MORTIMER
It's a metaphor.

DUNCAN
For what?

MORTIMER
For paddling.

LAKSHMI
Together.

MORTIMER
Exactly. Thank you, Lakshmi.

DUNCAN
I thought we were going to cancel the thing.

MORTIMER
What thing?

DUNCAN
The thing that the other thing replaced.

LAKSHMI
Duncan, that was the original thing.

DUNCAN
Oh.

MORTIMER
We don't cancel things. We sunset them.

LAKSHMI
Sunset them how?

MORTIMER
Gently. With a runway.

DUNCAN
What's at the end of the runway?

MORTIMER
Another meeting.

LAKSHMI
Of course it is.

DUNCAN
Do you have to be in the closet for this?

MORTIMER
The conference room is booked.

LAKSHMI
For what?

MORTIMER
A meeting about the closet.

DUNCAN
I need to get toner.

MORTIMER
Take whatever you need. This is a safe space.

LAKSHMI
It's a closet.

MORTIMER
A safe closet.

DUNCAN
Is anyone writing this down?

MORTIMER
No. That's the beauty of it.
